# This test loads the real terrain/climate fixture project
# (projects/test - real elevation/texture/NAEFS/GEOMET data for
# Toronto, see projects/test/terrain/elevations.md and textures.md) and
# shows the real terrain mesh, terrain texture, NAEFS ensemble-forecast
# data, and GEOMET troposphere tile it provides.

# RunStamp (globalVariables.pde) defaults to the real system clock at
# startup, and Folder_GEOMET (updateFolders.pde) is built from it - but
# the real GEOMET fixture is a fixed, pre-captured subfolder
# (projects/test/data/GEOMET/20261113_23/), not "right now". RUN.STAMP
# overrides RunStamp directly so Folder_GEOMET resolves to that real
# subfolder once NEW below derives it - must run first, since NEW's own
# update_project_folders() call only derives Folder_GEOMET from
# whatever RunStamp already is at that moment.
RUN.STAMP 20261113_23

# NEW takes no existing file to work - it just points Folder_Project at
# the given path's own parent directory and clears the scene (see
# fileSelected.pde's own _fileSelected_New()); no "test.xml" needs to
# actually exist on disk. STATION's own bare-construction default
# (Toronto, 43.67,-79.63) already matches this fixture's own real
# coordinates (043669998_-079629997), so no separate station command is
# needed here.
New projects/test/test.xml

# default clear
Delete all

# Terrain Load Mesh's own OnChange (react.applyLandLoadMesh) is what
# actually calls Terrain.update_mesh() - only on a real change, so it's
# toggled off then back on here to force a fresh reload from the
# project just switched to, rather than relying on whatever (if
# anything) was already loaded.
Terrain Load Mesh 0
Terrain Load Mesh 1

# Terrain.skipStart's own bare-construction default is 1 (skips the
# innermost row); 0 includes it.
Terrain Skip Start 0

Terrain Display Surface 1
Terrain Display Texture 1

Earth3D Display Surface 0

# The real NAEFS fixture's own filenames are all timestamped
# 2026111300 (year/month/day/hour) - matching that here is what lets
# "Use Ensemble Forecast" below actually find and load them (its own
# update_ensembleForecast() builds each file's name from TIME.year/
# month/day/hour directly). TIME.hour's own bare-construction default
# is already 0 (TIME.modelRun's own default), so only year/month/day
# need setting.
Year 2026
Month 11
Day 13

# Loads every real NAEFS layer file that exists for that date (TMP-SFC/
# MSLP/RELH-SFC/APCP-SFC - projects/test/data/NAEFS/) AND switches
# STUDY's own current data source to it in the same step (currentDataSource/
# STUDY.daysMergedCount/the WORLD ensemble-forecast display flags - see
# actions.pde's own "Use Ensemble Forecast" action) - loading and
# showing in one real command, not two.
Use Ensemble Forecast

# Loads the real GEOMET troposphere tile from the now-correctly-
# resolved Folder_GEOMET (RUN.STAMP above) - already-downloaded files
# are reused as-is, not re-fetched (Tropo3D.download_images()'s own
# "if (!dir.isFile())" check) - and shows it (Tropo3D.displaySurface = true,
# part of this same action - see actions.pde's own "Load Toroposphere").
Load Toroposphere

Hide Sun Path

=======
S.W.
REC.png terrain-mesh-and-texture
=======
